/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  postDict -- the batch plan, sizing, costing and economics of the TWO-STRENGTH
  donepezil tablet plant: the 10 mg and the 5 mg film-coated tablets as TWO
  PRODUCTS in single-product campaigns on ONE solid-dose plant (DEV.md 4c
  C249).  The README is the narrative; this file is the declaration.

  WHAT THIS FILE DECLARES, IN ORDER
    batchPlan   two trains, two products, the campaign order, the clean
                between products (a default per stage, and a DIRECTION-
                DEPENDENT one at the stages that touch the yellow coat)
    cleaning    the water of one clean of each wet-cleaned machine, counted by
                the plan per product
    sizing      the two preparation vessels on the plan's volume (the larger
                product's: `sizingProduct`), the two air heaters, the seven
                machines checked against a declared rating for each product
    cleanUtilities  the air of each grade and the purified water
    costing     declared quotes, each labelled an author-set placeholder,
                that scale with the plan
    economics   the discounted cash flow, the declared operating crew, the
                price sensitivity, working capital and land

  THE THREE TOOLS OF donepezil01_tablets, NOW OVER TWO PRODUCTS (DEV.md 4c
  C249 d).  The engine counts the cleaning of the machines per product (a
  clean after every lot of each strength, at each campaign changeover and at
  each product changeover), checks every `ratedMachine` against EACH product's
  lot and operating time (the refusal names the product that does not fit),
  and draws the purified water per lot of each strength; the HVAC is
  room-based and does not depend on the mix.  The building is therefore priced
  as donepezil01_tablets prices it: 5240 EUR/m2 for the shell plus the two
  `hvacGrade` supply-air quotes.

  EVERY DESIGN NUMBER BELOW IS AN AUTHOR-SET ASSUMPTION, said on its line,
  for the group to replace; none cites a source because none was read, except
  where a `source` names a document that was.  MATERIAL SS316 everywhere
  (product contact); pressureDesign 2 bar (atmospheric tanks and air
  heaters); vessels with a fully radiographed joint, 1.5 mm corrosion
  allowance and L/D 1.5, declared so that no engine default is used silently.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

//  ======================== THE BATCH PLAN (DEV.md 4c C99, C110 G2, C249) ===
//  The flowsheet is the MATERIAL BALANCE PER UNIT OF PRODUCT, and here it is
//  the balance of BOTH strengths: the 5 mg tablet is the 10 mg tablet at half
//  the weight (the same blend, README section 1), so a kg of either carries
//  the same kg of every ingredient and the engine reads the one balance for
//  both (BatchPlanPass.H:189-193).  The one difference that would reach the
//  balance, the 1 % yellow iron oxide of the 10 mg coat, is 0.03 % of the
//  tablet and is ignored (README section 2); a declared `massPerProduct`
//  would be announced as `ownBalance` instead.
//
//  TWO TRAINS, decoupled by the FINAL-BLEND store (the blend is held in closed
//  bins for QC release before it is pressed): the granulation suite and the
//  tableting suite each run their own campaigns, and each is cleaned between
//  products.  The method is BatchPlanPass.H:157-230.
//
//  THE LOT is the 300 kg bin of final blend for BOTH strengths.  The same bin
//  holds 1.07 million 10 mg cores or 2.14 million 5 mg cores, so the 5 mg lot
//  runs on the press and on the packaging line TWICE AS LONG at the same
//  tablets an hour (the per-product `stages` below).  That is the one place
//  the two products differ in time, and it moves the limiting stage of the
//  tableting train.
//
//  THE ORDER of the campaigns, `campaignOrder`, is the student's decision; the
//  engine never takes it (BatchPlanPass.H:159-162).  With TWO products the
//  year does not depend on it: the plan wraps the clean after the last
//  campaign to the first product (BatchPlanPass.H:208-210), so both
//  directions are paid once whichever product goes first.  From three
//  products on the order matters, and only through the direction-dependent
//  cleans (BatchPlanPass.H:219-224).  README section 4 says so.
//
//  EVERY NUMBER BELOW IS AN AUTHOR-SET ASSUMPTION of the right order for a
//  commercial oral-solid-dose line, said so in each `source`.
batchPlan
{
    product   packagedTablets;

    //  Both strengths, in single-product campaigns on the same trains.  The
    //  demand is split in TABLETS first, because that is what a market buys,
    //  and converted to kg of packaged tablets at each tablet's mass.
    products
    (
        {
            product  strength10;
            perYear  26121 kg;     // 90 million 10 mg tablets x 0.29023 g
            //  ONE TABLET'S MASS: the plan counts the product in tablets and
            //  publishes each ingredient in mg per tablet (C264) -- the
            //  composition is the packaged-tablet stream's own, so this is
            //  the only number the count needs.
            dosageUnit
            {
                name    tablet;
                mass    0.29023 g;
                source  "donepezil01_tablets README section 2: the 280 mg core of the UK SmPC (ARICEPT 10 mg) with a 3 % film coat, packed";
                reason  "the 10 mg film-coated tablet this strength is sold as";
            }
            //  THE CLEAN AFTER THE YELLOW 10 mg, BEFORE THE WHITE 5 mg: the
            //  longer one.  A trace of yellow iron oxide (E172) left in the
            //  coating suspension tank, the spray lines and the perforated pan
            //  shows as yellow specks on white tablets, and the cleaning is
            //  validated to a limit the white product's appearance sets.  The
            //  clean the other way, white then yellow, hides a trace of
            //  titanium dioxide in a yellow coat that already carries it.
            stages
            (
                { stage suspensionPreparation;  changeoverTo { strength5 32 h; }   // 24 h campaign clean + 8 h
                  source "author-set assumption, not a cleaning-validation result";
                  reason "colour carry-over: the yellow pigment of the 10 mg suspension must be rinsed out of the tank, the pump and the lines before the white 5 mg coat; one more rinse and a visual-clean check than the other direction"; }
                { stage coating;  changeoverTo { strength5 36 h; }   // 24 h campaign clean + 12 h
                  source "author-set assumption, not a cleaning-validation result";
                  reason "colour carry-over: the perforated pan, the spray guns and the exhaust ductwork hold yellow iron oxide that would speck a white coat; a full wet clean with a swab/rinse check is the longest clean of the plant"; }
            );
            source   "author-set market assumption, not a market study: 90 million 10 mg tablets a year (three fifths of 150 million, donepezil01_tablets' total), at the packed tablet's 0.29023 g (donepezil01_tablets README section 2) = 26 121 kg";
            reason   "the higher-volume strength of a dose-escalation pair: a patient starts on 5 mg and most are maintained on 10 mg; the split is the group's market study to replace";
        }
        {
            product  strength5;
            perYear  8707 kg;      // 60 million 5 mg tablets x 0.145115 g
            dosageUnit
            {
                name    tablet;
                mass    0.145115 g;
                source  "README section 2: half the 10 mg tablet (one blend pressed at two weights, an inference from the two SmPCs' lactose ratio)";
                reason  "the 5 mg film-coated tablet this strength is sold as";
            }
            //  The 5 mg tablet is the 10 mg tablet at half the weight, so the
            //  same 300 kg bin makes twice the tablets: the press and the
            //  packaging line run twice as long (7 h -> 14 h, 9 h -> 18 h) at
            //  their own tablet rates.
            stages
            (
                { stage compression;  operatingTime 14 h;
                  source "arithmetic on this case's own press time: 2.14 million cores at the same 150 000 tablets an hour that gives the 10 mg lot's 7 h (donepezil01_tablets postDict)";
                  reason "the 5 mg core is half the mass, so a 300 kg bin holds twice the cores; the press is rated in tablets an hour"; }
                { stage packaging;  operatingTime 18 h;
                  source "arithmetic on this case's own line time: twice the tablets at the same 120 000 an hour that gives the 10 mg lot's 9 h (donepezil01_tablets postDict)";
                  reason "twice the tablets in a 300 kg lot, on a line rated in tablets a minute"; }
                //  THE CLEAN AFTER THE WHITE 5 mg, BEFORE THE YELLOW 10 mg:
                //  the shorter one (see strength10 above).
                { stage suspensionPreparation;  changeoverTo { strength10 27 h; }   // 24 h campaign clean + 3 h
                  source "author-set assumption, not a cleaning-validation result";
                  reason "the white suspension leaves only titanium dioxide, which the yellow coat already contains: a rinse on top of the campaign clean is enough"; }
                { stage coating;  changeoverTo { strength10 30 h; }   // 24 h campaign clean + 6 h
                  source "author-set assumption, not a cleaning-validation result";
                  reason "the pan is washed and checked for residue, but a trace of white pigment is invisible in the yellow coat: half the increment the other direction needs"; }
            );
            source   "author-set market assumption, not a market study: 60 million 5 mg tablets a year (two fifths of 150 million), at the packed tablet's 0.145115 g = half of the 10 mg tablet's (the SmPCs' half-weight pair, README section 1) = 8 707 kg";
            reason   "the starting dose and the lower-volume strength; the split is the group's market study to replace";
        }
    );
    campaignOrder ( strength10 strength5 );

    lot
    {
        rule     declared;
        stream   finalBlend;
        mass     300 kg;
        source   "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C110), not a validated lot size";
        reason   "a commercial wet-granulation lot of a few hundred kg of blend, granulated and dried in one load, for BOTH strengths: one bin, one blender, one granulation lot size; the lot is what QC releases, so its size is a regulatory as well as an equipment choice";
    }

    lowUtilisation  0.25;       // a stage below a quarter of its cycle is announced

    trains
    (
        {
            train           granulation;
            availableTime   3840 h;     // 2 shifts x 8 h x 5 days x 48 weeks
            lotsPerCampaign 8;
            changeover      24 h;       // a full clean of the suite and its line clearance, between campaigns of ONE product
            source  "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C110)";
            reason  "a wet-granulation suite on two day shifts, a product campaign of eight lots between full cleans";
        }
        {
            train           tableting;
            availableTime   3840 h;     // 2 shifts x 8 h x 5 days x 48 weeks
            lotsPerCampaign 8;
            changeover      24 h;
            source  "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C110)";
            reason  "compression, coating and packaging on two day shifts, campaigns of eight lots between full cleans";
        }
    );

    //  THE CLEANING OF THE MACHINES (DEV.md 4c C210, E3).  The plan counts the
    //  cleans -- one after every lot of each instance the lot is split over, and
    //  one of every installed instance at each campaign changeover -- and the
    //  CASE declares the purified water of ONE clean of ONE instance and the
    //  fraction of it that leaves as effluent.  EVERY NUMBER IS AN AUTHOR-SET
    //  ASSUMPTION, round figures of the right order, to be replaced by the
    //  group's cleaning procedure (a rinse volume per wet-cleaned item).  The
    //  mill, the press and the packaging line are DRY-cleaned (vacuum and
    //  wipe-down): they carry no water and are not listed.  The purified-water
    //  demand of `cleanUtilities` reads these cleans (one ledger: the old lump
    //  `uses` entry `cleaning` is gone), and the effluent is published as a
    //  VOLUME in m3 a year (`kpis.cleaning`), its load is not computed.
    cleaning
    (
        { unit binderPrep;            waterPerLotClean 0.2 m3;  waterPerChangeover 0.5 m3;  effluentFraction 0.95;
          source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C210, E3), to be replaced by the group's cleaning procedure";
          reason "a rinse of the binder tank and its transfer line after each lot; a full rinse at a changeover"; }
        { unit granulator;            waterPerLotClean 0.8 m3;  waterPerChangeover 2.0 m3;  effluentFraction 0.95;
          source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C210, E3), to be replaced by the group's cleaning procedure";
          reason "the wet wash of the high-shear bowl, impeller and chopper after a lot; a full clean with detergent at a changeover"; }
        { unit fluidBedDryer;         waterPerLotClean 0.6 m3;  waterPerChangeover 1.5 m3;  effluentFraction 0.95;
          source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C210, E3), to be replaced by the group's cleaning procedure";
          reason "the wash of the product bowl and the filter housing after a lot (the filter bags are dry-cleaned or changed); a full clean at a changeover"; }
        { unit finalBlender;          waterPerLotClean 0.2 m3;  waterPerChangeover 0.5 m3;  effluentFraction 0.95;
          source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C210, E3), to be replaced by the group's cleaning procedure";
          reason "a rinse of the bin blender after the lubricated blend; a full clean at a changeover"; }
        { unit coatingSuspensionPrep; waterPerLotClean 0.3 m3;  waterPerChangeover 0.8 m3;  effluentFraction 0.95;
          source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C210, E3), to be replaced by the group's cleaning procedure";
          reason "a rinse of the coating suspension tank and the spray lines after each lot; a full clean at a changeover"; }
        { unit coatingPan;            waterPerLotClean 0.9 m3;  waterPerChangeover 2.0 m3;  effluentFraction 0.95;
          source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C210, E3), to be replaced by the group's cleaning procedure";
          reason "the wash of the perforated pan, the spray guns and the lines after a coated lot; a full clean at a changeover"; }
    );

    //  In RECIPE order; each stage feeds the next of its train unless it
    //  says otherwise.  `holds` names the stream whose flowsheet mass the
    //  stage handles per lot -- the mass is READ, never typed here.
    //  `productChangeover` is the clean between campaigns of DIFFERENT
    //  products at that stage (the products' `changeoverTo` override it where
    //  the direction matters): the train's 24 h campaign clean PLUS the
    //  product's own part, never less (DEV.md 4c C389).  THE SAME API in both
    //  strengths: the increments are line clearance (no strength mixed up) and
    //  the colour of the coat, smaller than a change between two APIs.
    stages
    (
        //  ---- train granulation ----------------------------------------
        {
            stage  binderPreparation;  train granulation;  type batch;
            units  ( binderPrep );     holds binderSolution;
            bulkDensity  1020 kg/m3;   // a 10 wt % HPC solution in water
            fillFraction 0.8;
            chargeTime   0.5 h;  processTime 1 h;  cleanTime 1 h;
            dischargeTime throughFedStage;   // pumped into the granulator while it granulates
            productChangeover 26 h;          // 24 h campaign clean + 2 h
            source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C110); the density is water's, rounded up for the polymer; the product change is the train's 24 h campaign clean plus 2 h of rinse and line-clearance check, an assumption";
            reason "one tank of binder solution per lot, held until the granulator has taken it";
        }
        {
            stage  granulation;  train granulation;  type batch;
            units  ( granulator );  holds wetMass;
            bulkDensity  550 kg/m3;  fillFraction 0.6;   // a high-shear bowl at 60 % of its volume
            chargeTime 0.5 h;  processTime 0.5 h;  dischargeTime 0.25 h;  cleanTime 1.5 h;
            productChangeover 30 h;          // 24 h campaign clean + 6 h
            source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C110), not a measured bulk density; the product change is the train's 24 h campaign clean plus 6 h for the rinse check of bowl, impeller and chopper against the other strength, an assumption";
            reason "dry mixing, binder addition and wet massing in one load; discharged wet straight into the fluid-bed bowl";
        }
        {
            stage  drying;  train granulation;  type batch;
            units  ( fluidBedDryer fbdAirHeater );  holds wetMass;
            bulkDensity  550 kg/m3;  fillFraction 0.5;   // the bowl, with room for the bed to expand
            chargeTime 0.25 h;  processTime 1.5 h;  dischargeTime 0.5 h;  cleanTime 2 h;
            productChangeover 29 h;          // 24 h campaign clean + 5 h
            source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C110); the 1.5 h is the drying time the flowsheet basis is built on (system/flowsheetDict); the product change is the train's 24 h campaign clean plus 5 h for the filter-bag change and its check, an assumption";
            reason "the wet mass dried in one load to its end-point moisture, then cooled with ambient air and discharged";
        }
        {
            stage  milling;  train granulation;  type semicontinuous;
            units  ( mill );  holds driedGranules;
            chargeTime 0.25 h;  operatingTime 2 h;  dischargeTime 0 h;  cleanTime 1 h;
            productChangeover 26 h;          // 24 h campaign clean + 2 h
            source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C110); the product change is the train's 24 h campaign clean plus 2 h of dry clean (vacuum and wipe-down) and its check, an assumption";
            reason "the dried granules sized through a screen mill into the blending bin";
        }
        {
            stage  finalBlending;  train granulation;  type batch;
            units  ( finalBlender );  holds finalBlend;
            bulkDensity  500 kg/m3;  fillFraction 0.6;
            chargeTime 0.5 h;  processTime 0.25 h;  dischargeTime 0.5 h;  cleanTime 1 h;
            productChangeover 27 h;          // 24 h campaign clean + 3 h
            source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C110); the product change is the train's 24 h campaign clean plus 3 h of rinse of the bin blender and the bins, an assumption";
            reason "the lubricant blended in for a few minutes in a bin blender; the bin is the lot's store until release";
        }

        //  ---- train tableting ----------------------------------------------
        {
            stage  compression;  train tableting;  type semicontinuous;
            units  ( tabletPress );  holds finalBlend;
            feeds  coating;
            chargeTime 1.5 h;  operatingTime 7 h;  dischargeTime 0 h;  cleanTime 1.5 h;
            productChangeover 28 h;          // 24 h campaign clean + 4 h
            source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C110); the product change is the train's 24 h campaign clean plus 4 h to change the tooling to the other strength's punches and dies, an assumption";
            reason "a rotary press set up for the lot (tooling, weight and hardness checks) and run at about 150 000 tablets an hour (the 10 mg lot; the 5 mg lot runs 14 h)";
        }
        {
            stage  suspensionPreparation;  train tableting;  type batch;
            units  ( coatingSuspensionPrep );  holds coatingSuspension;
            feeds  coating;
            bulkDensity  1050 kg/m3;  fillFraction 0.7;
            chargeTime 0.5 h;  processTime 1.5 h;  cleanTime 0.5 h;
            dischargeTime throughFedStage;   // sprayed onto the cores through the coating
            productChangeover 27 h;          // 24 h + 3 h; overridden by each product's changeoverTo (colour)
            source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C110); the density is of the order of a 12 wt % pigmented HPMC suspension";
            reason "the coating suspension is made for each lot and sprayed while the pan coats";
        }
        {
            stage  coating;  train tableting;  type batch;
            units  ( coatingPan coatingDryer coatingAirHeater );  holds tabletCores;
            bulkDensity  750 kg/m3;  fillFraction 0.65;   // tablet bed in a perforated pan
            chargeTime 0.5 h;  processTime 4 h;  dischargeTime 0.5 h;  cleanTime 1.5 h;
            productChangeover 30 h;          // 24 h + 6 h; overridden by each product's changeoverTo (colour)
            source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C110)";
            reason "one lot of cores coated in one pan load to a 3 % weight gain";
        }
        {
            stage  packaging;  train tableting;  type semicontinuous;
            units  ( packagingLine );  holds packagedTablets;
            chargeTime 1 h;  operatingTime 9 h;  dischargeTime 0 h;  cleanTime 1 h;
            productChangeover 28 h;          // 24 h campaign clean + 4 h
            source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C110); the product change is the train's 24 h campaign clean plus 4 h of line clearance of printed foil, cartons and leaflets of the other strength (no strength mixed up), an assumption";
            reason "a PVC/aluminium blister line (the reference product's pack, SmPC section 6.5) set up and cleared for each lot, run at about 120 000 tablets an hour (the 10 mg lot; the 5 mg lot runs 18 h)";
        }
    );
}

sizing
{
    units
    (
        //  ---- the two air heaters: A = Q/(U LMTD), LMTD computed against
        //  the utility record; U is a gas-side film against condensing
        //  steam -- ASSUMED.
        { unitName fbdAirHeater;  type shellTubeHX;  material SS316;
          designRules { utility steamLP;  U 40;  pressureDesign 2; } }
        { unitName coatingAirHeater;  type shellTubeHX;  material SS316;
          designRules { utility steamLP;  U 40;  pressureDesign 2; } }

        //  ---- the two preparation tanks, sized by the BATCH PLAN ---------
        //  `volume fromBatchPlan;`: each holds one lot of its liquid, V = S B.
        { unitName binderPrep;  type vessel;  material SS316;
          designRules { volume fromBatchPlan;  L_over_D 1.5;  pressureDesign 2;
                        corrosionAllow 0.0015;  jointEfficiency 1.0; } }
        { unitName coatingSuspensionPrep;  type vessel;  material SS316;
          designRules { volume fromBatchPlan;  L_over_D 1.5;  pressureDesign 2;
                        corrosionAllow 0.0015;  jointEfficiency 1.0; } }

        //  ---- THE SOLID-DOSE MACHINES, RATED (DEV.md 4c C195) --------------
        //  Each machine the flowsheet carries as a mass-balance placeholder is
        //  checked against a DECLARED rating and the batch plan's lot:
        //  utilisation = load / (machines x rating).  EVERY rating below is
        //  an author-set assumption for the group to replace with a data
        //  sheet.  The item is not costed (the quote below carries the money)
        //  and not placed (its ROOM is what the plot plan places).
        { unitName granulator;  type ratedMachine;  material SS316;
          designRules
          {
              kind batchVolume;
              rating
              {
                       nominalVolume 1.2 m3;
                       maxFill 0.6;
                       source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C195), not a vendor data sheet: a high-shear granulator bowl of about a cubic metre";
                       reason "the dry powders, the binder and the wet mass of one lot in one bowl";
              }
              shift { length 8 h;
                      source "README section 2a / the batch plan: the solid-dose suite runs two day shifts of 8 h (system/postDict, train availableTime)";
                      reason "a lot that cannot be finished inside the shift it starts in spans shifts, a staffing and GMP line-clearance question"; }
          } }
        { unitName fluidBedDryer;  type ratedMachine;  material SS316;
          designRules
          {
              kind batchVolume;
              rating
              {
                       nominalVolume 1.5 m3;
                       maxFill 0.5;
                       source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C195), not a vendor data sheet: a fluid-bed product bowl; the largest fill leaves room for the bed to expand";
                       reason "the wet mass of one lot dried in one load";
              }
              shift { length 8 h;
                      source "README section 2a / the batch plan: the solid-dose suite runs two day shifts of 8 h (system/postDict, train availableTime)";
                      reason "a lot that cannot be finished inside the shift it starts in spans shifts, a staffing and GMP line-clearance question"; }
          } }
        { unitName mill;  type ratedMachine;  material SS316;
          designRules
          {
              kind massRate;
              rating
              {
                       capacity 500 kg/h;
                       source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C195), not a vendor data sheet: a conical screen mill";
                       reason "the dried granules sized through a screen; replace with the mill's data sheet";
              }
              shift { length 8 h;
                      source "README section 2a / the batch plan: the solid-dose suite runs two day shifts of 8 h (system/postDict, train availableTime)";
                      reason "a lot that cannot be finished inside the shift it starts in spans shifts, a staffing and GMP line-clearance question"; }
          } }
        { unitName finalBlender;  type ratedMachine;  material SS316;
          designRules
          {
              kind batchVolume;
              rating
              {
                       nominalVolume 1.0 m3;
                       maxFill 0.7;
                       source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C195), not a vendor data sheet: a bin blender and its bin";
                       reason "the 300 kg final-blend lot of the case in one bin";
              }
              shift { length 8 h;
                      source "README section 2a / the batch plan: the solid-dose suite runs two day shifts of 8 h (system/postDict, train availableTime)";
                      reason "a lot that cannot be finished inside the shift it starts in spans shifts, a staffing and GMP line-clearance question"; }
          } }
        { unitName tabletPress;  type ratedMachine;  material SS316;
          designRules
          {
              kind tabletPress;
              rating
              {
                       stations 55;
                       turretSpeed 60;
                       compressionsPerRevolution 1;
                       itemMass 0.28 g;
                       itemMassByProduct { strength5 0.14 g; }   // the 5 mg core is the 10 mg core at half the weight (README section 1)
                       source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C195), not a vendor data sheet: a rotary press, 55 stations at 60 rpm, single-sided, nameplate with no efficiency applied; the pressed core is the 280 mg of the case (README section 2)";
                       reason "a mid-size rotary press; replace with the press vendor's data sheet and tooling";
              }
              shift { length 8 h;
                      source "README section 2a / the batch plan: the solid-dose suite runs two day shifts of 8 h (system/postDict, train availableTime)";
                      reason "a lot that cannot be finished inside the shift it starts in spans shifts, a staffing and GMP line-clearance question"; }
          } }
        { unitName coatingPan;  type ratedMachine;  material SS316;
          designRules
          {
              kind batchVolume;
              rating
              {
                       nominalVolume 1.0 m3;
                       maxFill 0.65;
                       source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C195), not a vendor data sheet: a perforated coating pan of about a cubic metre";
                       reason "one lot of cores in one pan load";
              }
              shift { length 8 h;
                      source "README section 2a / the batch plan: the solid-dose suite runs two day shifts of 8 h (system/postDict, train availableTime)";
                      reason "a lot that cannot be finished inside the shift it starts in spans shifts, a staffing and GMP line-clearance question"; }
          } }
        { unitName packagingLine;  type ratedMachine;  material SS316;
          designRules
          {
              kind packagingLine;
              rating
              {
                       packsPerMinute 100;
                       itemsPerPack 28;
                       itemMass 0.29023 g;
                       itemMassByProduct { strength5 0.145115 g; }   // the packed 5 mg tablet: half the 10 mg tablet
                       source "author-set assumption (DEV.md 4c C195), not a vendor data sheet: a blister line at 100 blisters of 28 tablets a minute; the packed tablet is the 0.29023 g of the case";
                       reason "a PVC/aluminium blister line at its nameplate speed; replace with the packaging vendor's data sheet";
              }
